 🔟 Message vs Event in Saga (Final Verdict)

| Use           | Use This          |
|---------------|-------------------|
| Start Saga    | Command / Message |
| Progress Saga | Events            |
| Notify Others | Events            |
| Compensations | Commands          |

📌 Best practice:
> Hybrid model — Commands internally, Events externally

 1️⃣1️⃣ Interview-Ready Answer

> Saga is typically implemented using event-driven choreography, where services publish domain events after local transactions. 
	Message-based orchestration is also possible but leads to tighter coupling and reduced scalability.

